{
  "id": "Lyo.Authentication.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Authentication.Postgres",
  "area": "Security",
  "tagline": "PostgreSQL persistence for `Lyo.Authentication`. Replaces the in-memory stores from the base lib with EF Core-backed implementations of `IApiTokenStore`, `IUserStore`, and `IExternalIdentityStore`.",
  "description": "PostgreSQL persistence for `Lyo.Authentication`. Replaces the in-memory stores from the base lib with EF Core-backed implementations of `IApiTokenStore`, `IUserStore`, and `IExternalIdentityStore`.\n\nOwns the `[user]` schema. Four tables in this lib:\n\n- `[user].[user]` — Lyo internal users - `[user].[token]` — Format-B opaque API tokens - `[user].[linked_identity]` — external OIDC identity links - `[user].[event]` — auth audit events (`UserEventEntity`)\n\n`__EFMigrationsHistory` lives inside the `[user]` schema.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register services",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddLyoAuthentication();\nservices.AddPostgresAuthenticationStoresFromConfiguration(configuration);"
    },
    {
      "title": "Register services (2)",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPostgresApiTokenStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddPostgresUserStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddPostgresExternalIdentityStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);"
    },
    {
      "title": "Register services (3)",
      "language": "json",
      "code": "{\n  \"PostgresUser\": {\n    \"ConnectionString\": \"Host=...;Database=lyo;...\",\n    \"EnableAutoMigrations\": true\n  }\n}"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Registration",
      "text": "Or each store individually: `appsettings.json`:"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "Tenancy",
      "body": "All four entities (`UserEntity`, `TokenEntity`, `LinkedIdentityEntity`, `UserEventEntity`) carry a nullable `tenant_id` (uuid) column with filtered indexes\n(`ix_<table>_tenant_id`). `null` represents cross-tenant / system records; non-null values scope the row to a specific tenant. Unique constraints on\n`UserEntity.Email` and `LinkedIdentityEntity (provider, subject)` include `tenant_id`, so the same email or external subject can exist per tenant.\n\n`IUserStore`, `IApiTokenStore`, `IExternalIdentityStore`, and `PostgresAuthAuditRecorder` all accept an explicit `Guid? tenantId` and run it through\n`TenancyResolver.Resolve` using the policy configured in `PostgresUserOptions.Tenancy` (inheriting from `EntityRefOptions.Mode` when unset):\n\n- `SystemOnly` — every row is persisted with `tenant_id = NULL` and reads filter to system rows.\n- `SingleTenantDefault` *(default)* — caller value, falling back to `Tenancy.DefaultTenantId` then `EntityRefOptions.DefaultTenantId`.\n- `MultiTenantStrict` — caller must supply a non-empty `tenantId`; otherwise the store throws `ArgumentNullException` (the audit recorder swallows and logs).\n\nSee [`Lyo.EntityReference.Postgres` — Tenancy](../../../Core/EntityReference/Lyo.EntityReference.Postgres/README.md#tenancy) for the full matrix.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"PostgresUser\": {\n    \"ConnectionString\": \"Host=localhost;Database=auth;...\",\n    \"Tenancy\": { \"Mode\": \"MultiTenantStrict\" }\n  }\n}\n```"
    }
  ],
